## Code samples

### curl

```sh
curl '{{base_url}}/form' --data-raw 'q=a+b%26c&page={{page}}' -L
```

### httpie

```sh
http --ignore-stdin --follow '--raw=q=a+b%26c&page={{page}}' -- POST '{{base_url}}/form' \
  'Content-Type:application/x-www-form-urlencoded'
```

### fetch

```js
const BASE_URL = "{{base_url}}";
const PAGE = "{{page}}";

const response = await fetch(BASE_URL + "/form", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: {
    "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded",
  },
  body: "q=a+b%26c&page=" + PAGE,
});
console.log(response.status);
console.log(await response.text());
```

### python

```python
import requests

BASE_URL = "{{base_url}}"
PAGE = "{{page}}"

response = requests.post(
    BASE_URL + "/form",
    data=("q=a+b%26c&page=" + PAGE).encode(),
    headers={
        "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded",
    },
)
print(response.status_code)
print(response.text)
```

### rust

```rust
// Cargo.toml: reqwest = { version = "0.12", features = ["blocking"] }

const BASE_URL: &str = "{{base_url}}";
const PAGE: &str = "{{page}}";

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let client = reqwest::blocking::Client::builder()
        .build()?;
    let response = client
        .request(reqwest::Method::POST, [BASE_URL, "/form"].concat())
        .header("Content-Type", "application/x-www-form-urlencoded")
        .body(["q=a+b%26c&page=", PAGE].concat())
        .send()?;
    println!("{}", response.status());
    println!("{}", response.text()?);
    Ok(())
}
```
